#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: %(url) as RHS of assignment
#====================================================================


# design decisions for Section 30 (%fetch long + %(url) short forms):
#
#   `%fetch(url)` is a plain subscript on the sys receiver — same shape as
#   any `%name[key]` subscript:
#     [{sys: "puck"}, "[]", {args: [url_expr]}]
#
#   `%(url)` short form is a DISTINCT atom so tooling can tell the two source
#   forms apart. The atom is `{puck: {args: [...], kw: [...]}}` — the args
#   envelope mirrors the method-call `{args, kw}` convention. Kwargs use the
#   same `[[key, value_atom], ...]` shape as bwc-call kwargs (Section 12).
#   Empty `%()` raises.
#
#   Both forms accept a chained method call on the result:
#     %fetch(url).method(args)                     -> nested method-call shape
#     %(url).method(args)                         -> nested method-call shape
#     %(url, kwarg:val).method(args)              -> same
#   The fetch atom can appear anywhere a value-atom does: statement, RHS,
#   arg-list, method receiver.

#====================================================================
# Multi-key subscript lookups and assignments
#====================================================================


#====================================================================
# name: multi-key subscript get
# string, integer, and variable keys
#

#--- code -----------------------------------------------------------
$foo['bar', 2, $gup]
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- full -----------------------------------------------------------
[
	[
		{
			"var": "foo"
		},
		"[]",
		{
			"args": [
				{
					"line": 1,
					"value": "bar"
				},
				{
					"line": 1,
					"value": 2
				},
				{
					"line": 1,
					"var": "gup"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"line": 1
		}
	]
]
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#--- norm -----------------------------------------------------------
[
	[
		{
			"in": "fc"
		},
		{
			"a": [
				{
					"l": 1,
					"v": "bar"
				},
				{
					"l": 1,
					"v": 2
				},
				{
					"l": 1,
					"var": "gup"
				}
			],
			"fn": "[]",
			"rc": {
				"var": "foo"
			}
		}
	]
]
#--------------------------------------------------------------------

