#--------------------------------------------------------------------

#
# name: null-safe get as RHS of assignment
#====================================================================


# design decisions for Section 28 (multi-key subscript):
#
#   Multi-key subscript `recv[k1, k2, ..., kN]` transpiles as a `[]` method
#   call with all keys in the args list:
#     [recv, "[]", {args: [k1, k2, ..., kN]}]
#
#   Multi-key subscript assign `recv[k1, k2, ..., kN] = value` puts all keys
#   first, value last:
#     [recv, "[]=", {args: [k1, k2, ..., kN, value]}]
#
#   Same shape whether single-key or multi-key — no distinct atom for the
#   arity. Runtime dispatches on args count.
#
#   Empty subscript `recv[]` is a parse error (no meaningful semantics).
#
#   Null-safe form: a trailing `?` immediately after the closing bracket
#   switches the subscript to null-safe mode. Distinct method names carry
#   the intent through to the runtime:
#     $recv[k1, ..., kN]?             -> [recv, "[]?",  {args: [k1, ..., kN]}]
#     $recv[k1, ..., kN]? = value     -> [recv, "[]?=", {args: [k1, ..., kN, value]}]
#   Same shape for single-key and multi-key. Full semantic spec at
#   https://puck.uno/requirements/syntax/subscripts.

